  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ffu - Fisheries Intelligence and MCS support in West Africa phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective is strengthened governance and increased compliance with national and international laws related to fisheries operations in West Africa, contributing to the conservation and optimum use of living marine resources.
In the Gulf of Guinea, Illegal fishing accounts for a significant share of the catches and therefore affect jobs creation and contribute to poverty increase in fishing communities which are responding in various ways to the impacts of illegal fishing and declining fish stocks. Through the Fisheries Committee for the West Central Gulf of Guinea (FCWC), the countries of Liberia, C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, Ghana, Togo, Benin, and Nigeria, work to ensure a sustainable development of the fisheries resources in the FCWC Convention Area. The project proposal builds on the foundations and progress made to date under previous phase to specifically meet these objectives:
Outcome 1 - FCWC Member States are cooperating and effectively acting to reduce illegal fishing and associated crimes at the national, regional, and international level
Outcome 2 &#x2013; The FCWC is effectively achieving its mandate to promote cooperation among its Member States to ensure the conservation and optimum use of their living marine resources</narrative>
  </description>
